# Example demo-app.env

## Purpose
- This file provides an example of the environment variables required for the application to start and operate correctly, along with example values.

## Environment Variables
- APP_HOST=127.0.0.1
- APP_PORT=8080
- APP_DATA_DIR=/mnt/data-demo/demo-app

## Variable Descriptions
- APP_HOST — IP address of the interface on which the application listens for incoming connections.
- APP_PORT — TCP port on which the application listens for incoming connections.
- APP_DATA_DIR — absolute path to the directory where the application stores persistent data.

## Parameter Changes
- All three values can be changed depending on the deployment configuration:
    APP_HOST — depending on the network configuration and how the application is accessed.
    APP_PORT — provided that the selected TCP port is available and the configuration of interacting components is updated accordingly.
    APP_DATA_DIR — provided that the directory exists and the application user has the necessary permissions.

## Data Directory Requirements
- At startup, the application checks whether the APP_DATA_DIR directory exists and whether it is writable. The directory must be created in advance. The user running the application must have write permissions.
- During this check, the application creates the app-01.txt file if it does not already exist, or appends a startup entry to the existing file.

## Project-Specific Values
- The following values are used in this example:
    APP_HOST=127.0.0.1
    APP_PORT=8080
    APP_DATA_DIR=/mnt/data-demo/demo-app

These values reflect the target deployment configuration for the application on the app-01 server behind Nginx.